      $VER: FPPGN (Scan w/ Entry Text), v1.00 (25-Oct-96) by Dotoran!
-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-
Disclaimer:
~~~~~~~~~~
    Originally, v0.2 was written by PMK, aka Peter Klein. Since Peter has
decided to go the IBM route, I'll be attempting to "take on" the continued
development/support of the files he has authored in the past.

What's it Do?
~~~~~~~~~~~~
    This little file was one Peter wrote back in 1994 that was tied into the
SCAN command inside the list areas, like Gfiles, PFiles, etc. that could be
used to redisplay the ENTRY text(???.entry) file right before displaying
the scanned data.

Installation:
~~~~~~~~~~~~
1. Copy the included "FPPGN/" directory to "pfiles:fpfiles/"(3.05c) or
   "doors:fpfiles/"(4.xx).

   NOTE: Dotoran released "FP" files reside in the "FPFiles/" directory,
         so as to keep them all together. It is highly recommended that
         you do the same, however if you opt NOT to, please make the
         appropriate changes to BBSMENU using your own selected <path>.

2. Load your BBSMENU file into a text editor, then do the following:

   If running a 3.05c version of CNet:
                ~~~~~
   Find the "Scan, List" command in Menu # 6; News/GFiles/Pfiles, then add
   the following to the END of the line, so it looks like this:

            Scan, List  | {#0<path>fppgn/fppgn}
                          ^
                      Control-Q

        NOTE: Replace <path> above with "pfiles:fpfiles/" if you have one,
              or else use whichever path you DID choose to use.

    If running v4.23 or better CNet version:
               ~~~~~
    Find the "Scan" command in Menu # 4; The new Message/File Area menu,
    then add the following to the END of the line, so it looks like this:

            Scan        | {#0<path>fppgn/fppgn}
                          ^
                      Control-Q

        NOTE: Replace <path> above with "doors:fpfiles/" if you have one,
              or else use whichever path you DID choose to use.

3. That's It! Now reload your BBSMENU file and you'll be ready to use it!

History:
~~~~~~~
 -> 19 Sep 94 First Version.

 -> 20 Sep 94 Getuser 1306888 didn't return the expected value in G/P/N,
              after an item was selected. Now uses Getuser 1306644 for
              G/P/N.

 -> 25 Oct 96 Updated for use with both 3.05c and the newest 4.xx versions
              of CNet(4.24 as of this writing). First Dotoran release of
              this work.

